Found under k335 (destroy worker) and k331 (choices worker), 2026-10-31. validate() still has no line for these shapes, so every reader goes on with them:
- control_planes[n].public_ip / private_ip: a list there makes an ssh control plane's uninstall (destroy) and its address (apply) ARRAY(0x...).
- ssh: (private_key, public_key): a non-mapping ssh: dies inside Perl when destroy (and apply in dev mode) fetches the key -- destroy skips the uninstall, exits 1, prints the Perl error as the reason. Secrets lane reads it (ocp-secrets-worker for the reader side).
- system.timezone / system.locale that is a list or mapping passes validate() and reaches the Rexfile and the provider CR, whose CRD types both as strings.
- an empty or non-mapping ocp.yaml ends every command (destroy, apply alike) on "Not a HASH reference ... This is an internal error" -- one line naming the file would do.

Use k315's _not_a_string / _shown_value. Done = each is a validate() line (t/296 sweep), accessors agree, the three real configs (cihq, citiai, amdlab) still give 0 errors.

